{
  "summary": "Adds sync and lookup microbenchmarks for TxIndex, TxoSpenderIndex, and BlockFilterIndex, backed by shared utilities that generate synthetic blocks with chained spends and distinct output scripts. Also adds documentation to doc/benchmarking.md explaining how to measure I/O syscalls, peak resident memory, and disk usage using -testdatadir.",
  "problem": "Evaluating performance changes to the index subsystem previously required running a full initial block download (IBD). The only existing index benchmark, BlockFilterIndexSync, only processes blocks containing coinbase transactions, leaving no benchmarks for TxIndex or TxoSpenderIndex and no way to measure index scaling against transaction counts or distinct script outputs.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: The author notes that evaluating index changes previously required a full IBD, whereas this benchmark suite runs in under a minute.",
    "PR description: The author demonstrates its utility on PR #35531 (showing a 49% smaller index vs lookup regression) and PR #34489 (showing a 91% reduction in write syscalls with unchanged CPU)."
  ],
